This is a passive DWDM optical multiplexer/demultiplexer in a rack tray. The candidate headings are 9001 (optical elements), 8517.62 (machines for reception/conversion/transmission of data) and 8517.70 (parts of such apparatus).

I recall CBP rulings on passive optical MUX/DMUX modules that classified them as parts of telecom apparatus under 8517.70. A passive device with no active function is not itself a machine under 8517.62, so a parts provision fits better. 8517.70.00 is the parts provision, and the 10-digit statistical number 8517.70.0090 (other parts) seems right. The alternative, 8517.70.0030 (antennas), does not apply. I believe the 8517.70.00 subdivisions are 8517.70.0030 (antennas and antenna reflectors), 8517.70.0060 (of telephone sets, etc.) and 8517.70.0090 (other), so I'm using 8517.70.0090.

{"hts_code": "8517.70.0090", "reason": "A passive DWDM optical MUX/DMUX rack module used solely in telecommunications networks is classified as a part of telecom transmission apparatus under heading 8517, subheading 8517.70, in the 'other' parts provision."}
